Reverse a Linked List

Now we’ll learn one of the most important linked-list operations: reversing a linked list.

Suppose the original list is:

10 → 20 → 30 → 40 → None

After reversing:

40 → 30 → 20 → 10 → None

There are two common approaches:

Iterative method ⭐
Recursive method
1. Reverse Using the Iterative Method

The main idea is to change the direction of every next pointer.

